      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "On September 30, 1893, Postmaster George Ritchie opened a post office and the town was renamed Richfield.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://richfieldnc.gov/about/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town once had a train depot, a high school gym, a flour mill, and a hardware store where “you could buy a good rifle.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://richfieldnc.gov/about/history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After many fires, the community bought its first fire truck in 1956.",
